 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 518495,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "A simple interest loan for $24,200 is taken out at 10.55% annual percentage rate. A partial payment of $13,000 is made 25 days into the loan period. After this payment, what will the remaining balance of the loan be?\n\n",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Interest on the loan after 25 days:</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"I = P \\times r \\times t = 24,200 \\times 0.1055 \\times \\frac{{25}}{{365}} \\approx \\$ 174.43\"></span></td>\n<td>(rounded to the nearest cent)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Subtract the partial interest off the loan payment.</p>\n<p>$13,000 – 174.43 = $12,825.57 went toward paying off the loan.</p>\n<p>$24,200 – 12,825.57 = $11,374.43 is the remaining balance of the loan still due.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "$11,374.87"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
